[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Terraform Architecture and Core Workflow"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Terraform is an open-source infrastructure as code (IaC) software tool created by HashiCorp. It enables you to define and provision a datacenter infrastructure using a high-level configuration language known as HashiCorp Configuration Language (HCL)."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Terraform Core Architecture"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Terraform architecture is split into two primary components: Terraform Core and Providers. Understanding how these two components interact is essential for mastering infrastructure automation."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Terraform Core: Uses configuration files and state files to compute a plan for infrastructure changes. It reads inputs, manages the dependency graph, and orchestrates the execution."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Providers: Plugins that translate Terraform resource definitions into API calls for specific cloud platforms or services, such as AWS, Azure, GCP, or Kubernetes."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"The Core Workflow"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The standard Terraform workflow consists of three primary stages: Write, Plan, and Apply. Let us examine each phase in detail."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"1. Write: Author infrastructure as code in HCL using configuration files ending with the .tf extension."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"2. Plan: Preview the changes Terraform will make to match your configuration before actually applying them."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"3. Apply: Execute the planned changes to provision, update, or destroy infrastructure."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Step-by-Step Implementation"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Below is a sample configuration file (main.tf) that provisions a local file resource to demonstrate the workflow."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"terraform {
  required_providers {
    local = {
      source = "hashicorp/local"
      version = "~> 2.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "local" {}

resource "local_file" "sample" {
  content  = "Hello, Terraform Architecture!"
  filename = "output.txt"
}"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"To initialize the workspace and download the required provider plugins, run the init command in your terminal."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"terraform init"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"Next, generate and review the execution plan using the plan command."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"terraform plan"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"Finally, apply the configuration to create the resource."},{"order":20,"type":"code","text":"terraform apply -auto-approve"}]
